{"authored" [{"question" "q-102756" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\text{u}=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $\\text{v}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956518/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ec084eec6c9aa6624842d78db1774daef378db09bd606aea5a93a0b72890d48" "basis" 647 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956518/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-102756" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2} & 2 \\\\ 1 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2} & 2 \\\\ 1 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}-2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2-2 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of $det(M)$ gives the area $A$ of the parallelogram:\n\n$$\nA=|\\,0\\,|=0\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956518/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ec084eec6c9aa6624842d78db1774daef378db09bd606aea5a93a0b72890d48" "basis" 647 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956518/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-102756" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956518/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c2fd1b7355fa6c287086552bf692aa77ee3f50f827fa5efe6bbbbfbe23883039" "basis" 647 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956518/edb-i