rification.json"} {"question" "q-320394" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972686/assets/f63cf622acc15681e3815118bbd2a187ea6039a548d4be1773634c0dc450c343.png)\n\nDetermine the area $A$ of the parallelogram in the figure.\n\n$\\,\\,A=$ {{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972686/state.json" "file_sha256" "4292f151be1765de04a1018fa5eed494bc3f3018d87ba134b2b4ee95c91d0a34" "basis" 665 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972686/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-320394" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the diagram, we get the vectors\n\n$$\n\\text{u}=⟨4,-1⟩,\\,\\text{v}=⟨-2,-3⟩.\n$$\n\nFirst, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4\\cdot (-3)-(-2)\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-12-2 \\\\  & =-14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of $det(M)$ gives the area $A$ of the parallelogram:\n\n$$\nA=|-14|=14\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972686/state.json" "file_sha256" "4292f151be1765de04a1018fa5eed494bc3f3018d87ba134b2b4ee95c91d0a34" "basis" 665 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972686/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-320394" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972686/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "71a94be75fc9bf89f92e07f1bcc70a5c4dc33378bc2c8d6da1b46c650a6c7dae" "basis" 665 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972686/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-320394" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972686/state.json" "file_sha256" "4292f151be1765de04a1018fa5eed494bc3f3018d87ba134b2b4ee95c91d0a34" "basis" 665 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972686/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-275539" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine the area $A$ of the parallelogram spanned by $\\text{u}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ and $\\text{v}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n$\\,\\,A=$ {{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008824/state.json" "file_sha256" "d15b150f3a38fc3cbb41417ee5c1920ebb93691e27bb0c6208938a2ad22986f3" "basis" 1142 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008824/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-275539" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)-4\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of $det(M)$ gives the area $A$ of the parallelogram:\n\n$$\nA=|\\,-9\\,|=9\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008824/state.json" "file_sha256" "d15b150f3a38fc3cbb41417ee5c1920ebb93691e27bb0c6208938a2ad22986f3" "basis" 11