|\\,-9\\,|=9\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067751/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e9ae31c48f46ab7421552d63e95f2b44e244d45f40c2a6177bec57c570a9b12"} {"question" "q-275539" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067751/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "792aeec2deacf8f149484f3b58de9f3f296422d1972897f7cffefa4b3eec2049"} {"question" "q-275539" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067751/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e9ae31c48f46ab7421552d63e95f2b44e244d45f40c2a6177bec57c570a9b12"} {"question" "q-275539" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "9"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067751/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e9ae31c48f46ab7421552d63e95f2b44e244d45f40c2a6177bec57c570a9b12"} {"question" "q-320394" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067751/assets/f63cf622acc15681e3815118bbd2a187ea6039a548d4be1773634c0dc450c343.png)\n\nDetermine the area $A$ of the parallelogram in the figure.\n\n$\\,\\,A=$ {{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067751/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e9ae31c48f46ab7421552d63e95f2b44e244d45f40c2a6177bec57c570a9b12"} {"question" "q-320394" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the diagram, we get the vectors\n\n$$\n\\text{u}=⟨4,-1⟩,\\,\\text{v}=⟨-2,-3⟩.\n$$\n\nFirst, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4\\cdot (-3)-(-2)\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-12-2 \\\\  & =-14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of $det(M)$ gives the area $A$ of the parallelogram:\n\n$$\nA=|-14|=14\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067751/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e9ae31c48f46ab7421552d63e95f2b44e244d45f40c2a6177bec57c570a9b12"} {"question" "q-320394" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067751/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "792aeec2deacf8f149484f3b58de9f3f296422d1972897f7cffefa4b3eec2049"} {"question" "q-320394" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067751/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e9ae31c48f46ab7421552d63e95f2b44e244d45f40c2a6177bec57c570a9b12"} {"question" "q-320394" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "14"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067751/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e9ae31c48f46ab7421552d63e95f2b44e244d45f40c2a6177bec57c570a9b12"} {"question" "q-320412" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine the area $A$ of the parallelogram spanned by $\\text{u}=⟨2,7⟩$ and $\\text{v}=⟨-3,1⟩.$\n\n$\\,\\,A=$ {{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathac